  "nl_text": "The database schema, rschema_0494, is used to store information about users, articles, categories, and comments. The schema consists of four tables: user, article, category, and comment_reply.\nThe user table contains information about each user, including their user ID, username, password, nickname, gender, creation time, and biography. The user ID is the primary key for this table.\nThe article table contains information about each article, including its article ID, title, author ID, cover image link, summary, comment permission, status, content, number of likes, number of dislikes, number of reads, and creation time. The article ID is the primary key for this table.\nThe category table contains information about each category, including its ID, parent category ID, level, name, description, and icon link. The ID is the primary key for this table.\nThe comment_reply table contains information about each comment reply, including its comment ID, replied comment ID, article ID, user ID, content, and creation time. The comment ID is the primary key for this table.\nThe user table has a foreign key relationship with the article table, where the author ID in the article table references the user ID in the user table. The user table also has a foreign key relationship with the comment_reply table, where the user ID in the comment_reply table references the user ID in the user table.\nThe article table has a foreign key relationship with the category table, where the category ID in the article table references the ID in the category table. The article table also has a foreign key relationship with the comment_reply table, where the article ID in the comment_reply table references the article ID in the article table.\nThe category table has a foreign key relationship with itself, where the parent category ID in the category table references the ID in the category table.\nThe comment_reply table has a foreign key relationship with the article table, where the article ID in the comment_reply table references the article ID in the article table. The comment_reply table also has a foreign key relationship with the user table, where the user ID in the comment_reply table references the user ID in the user table.\nIn summary, the rschema_0494 database schema is used to store information about users, articles, categories, and comments. The schema consists of four tables, each with its own set of columns and relationships with other tables. The primary keys and foreign keys are used to ensure data integrity and consistency across the tables.",
  "gold_question": "A content management system specification is as follows:\nThe system accommodates multiple users. User information includes User ID, Username, Password, Nickname, Gender, Creation Time, and Biography.      \nThe system contains multiple articles. Article information includes Article ID, Title, Author, Cover Image Link, Summary, Comment Permission, Status, Content, Number of Likes, Number of Dislikes, Number of Reads, and Creation Time.\nArticles can belong to multiple categories. Category information includes ID, Parent Category ID, Level, Name, Description, and Icon Link, supporting multi-level classification.\nUsers can comment on articles. Comment information includes Comment ID, Replied Comment ID, Article ID, User ID, Content, and Creation Time.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0494.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0494\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `nickname` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `biography` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `article` (\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `cover_image_link` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `summary` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `comment_permission` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `likes` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `dislikes` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `reads` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`article_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `article_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`author_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `category` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `parent_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `level` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `icon_link` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `category_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`parent_id`) REFERENCES `category` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `comment_reply` (\n  `comment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `replied_comment_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`comment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `comment_reply_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`article_id`) REFERENCES `article` (`article_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comment_reply_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
